    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could act as adaptive tutors: flag missteps mid-step (e.g., ‘Your second guess was wrong—try x=1’), explain analogies (e.g., ‘Algebra is like a board game where pieces move predictably’) or generate practice problems based on weak areas. Their openness (score: moderate) could make them empathetic, turning math from rigid to playful."
